{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract methylation regions [-h] --build {hg38,t2t} --preset {promoters,cpg-islands}\n                                      [--upstream UPSTREAM] [--downstream DOWNSTREAM]\n                                      [--min-valid-calls MIN_VALID_CALLS] [--min-cpgs MIN_CPGS]\n                                      [--partition-hp] [--phase-blocks PHASE_BLOCKS] [--5hmc]\n                                      [--download] [--format {tsv,parquet}]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --build {hg38,t2t}    Assembly of both input and FASTA.\n  --preset {promoters,cpg-islands}\n                        RefSeq promoters or UCSC masked CpG islands.\n  --upstream UPSTREAM   Promoter bases upstream of the TSS (default: 2000).\n  --downstream DOWNSTREAM\n                        Promoter bases on the transcribed side (default: 500).\n  --min-valid-calls MIN_VALID_CALLS\n                        Minimum valid calls per CpG (default: 5).\n  --min-cpgs MIN_CPGS   Minimum qualifying CpGs per region (default: 3).\n  --partition-hp        Split CpG calls from HP-tagged BAM/CRAM (needs modkit on Linux or macOS).\n  --phase-blocks PHASE_BLOCKS\n                        Matching phased.blocks.tsv from vcf phase; require region containment in\n                        one block.\n  --5hmc                Also report 5hmC: declares the input was generated with a 5hmC-capable\n                        model.\n  --download            Fetch the missing pinned hg38 CpG island table from UCSC. No sample data\n                        is sent.\n  --format {tsv,parquet}\n                        Output table: tsv (default) or parquet (needs pyarrow).\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract methylation regions -i ont.cpg.bedmethyl.gz --ref hg38.fa --build hg38 --preset promoters\n  wgsextract methylation regions -i haplotagged.bam --ref hg38.fa --build hg38 --preset promoters --partition-hp --phase-blocks phased.blocks.tsv\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input stem>.<build>.<preset>.methylation.tsv (or .parquet) and its run\n  manifest. With --partition-hp, writes .methylation.hp.tsv (or .parquet)\n  instead.\n\nneeds:\n  samtools; depending on options and inputs, also: modkit, curl; minutes on a\n  30x genome.\n",
